<newsitem itemid="466965" id="root" date="1997-03-25" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Barclays creates 500 telephone bank jobs.</title>
<headline>Barclays creates 500 telephone bank jobs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Barclays Plc's Barclays Bank said on Tuesday it plans to create 500 full and part-time jobs in the North West of England in a new centre for its expanding Barclaycall telephone banking service.</p>
<p>The new call centre at Salford Quays, Manchester, will open later this year and up to 500 staff will be recruited locally over the next two years, Barclays said in a statement.</p>
<p>Barclays already has a call centre in the English Midlands at Coventry which employs 500 people.</p>
<p>Barclays said it has well over 300,000 customers in its 'phone bank and expects this number to double by the end of this year.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8864</p>
</text>
